The '''Nevarro school''', formerly the '''Nevarro Common House''' and briefly '''the Client's office''', was located in [[Nevarro City]] on the [[planet]] [[Nevarro]]. Originally a [[cantina]], it was built from [[Greef Karga]]'s cut of [[Gorian Shard]]'s treasure. The cantina was used by the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]].

==History==
===A thriving cantina===
{{Quote|You paid us for murder and mayhem inside these doors.|Vane to Greef Karga|<ref name="Chapter 17" />}}
During the [[New Republic Era]],<ref name="Chapter 1" /> the [[Nevarro]] Common House<ref name="The Mandalorian Handbook">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian Handbook]]''</ref> was a [[cantina]] that was the center of activity for the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] in [[Nevarro City]].<ref name="Chapter 1" /> It was built from [[Greef Karga]]'s cut of [[Gorian Shard]]'s treasure.<ref name="Chapter 17" /> Greef Karga gave out [[Bounty|bounties]] to [[Bounty hunter|members]] of the Bounty Hunters' Guild from the cantina. The location was frequently populated by a variety of patrons,<ref name="Chapter 1" /> including members of [[Gorian Shard's pirate crew|Gorian Shard's pirate gang]], who were paid for murder and mayhem.<ref name="Chapter 17" />

After the [[incident on Nevarro]], [[the Client]] turned the common house into his office.<ref name="Journey">{{InsiderCite|216|The Journey of Din Djarin}}</ref> The cantina was the site where the [[clash on Nevarro]] began, and it was heavily damaged, albeit not destroyed, by [[stormtrooper]] firing squads and an [[Incinerator stormtrooper|incinerator trooper]]&mdash;also resulting in the Client's death&mdash;before [[Din Djarin]], Karga, and their accomplices escaped the building.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

===Educational purposes===
{{Quote|A school?''"<br />"''Things have changed a lot around here.|Din Djarin and Cara Dune in what has become of the old common house|<ref name="Chapter 12">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 12: The Siege}}</ref>}}
At some point after Djarin left Nevarro, what remained of the cantina was converted<ref name="Chapter 12" /> into the Nevarro school<ref name="Art of Mando">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season Two)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Two]]</ref> for the children of the town as Karga and his new companion, ex-[[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune]], cleaned up the town in the aftermath of the Imperial presence. When Djarin returned to Nevarro to ask his friends Karga and Dune for their help, Djarin's companion [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] was left at the school during a lesson on geography of [[the galaxy]] while they went on a [[Second skirmish on Nevarro|mission]].<ref name="Chapter 12" />

===Showdown===
{{Quote|Let's continue this conversation back at my office. This, this is a school.|Greef Karga to Vane|<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>}}
Sometime later, pirates from Gorian Shard's gang arrived to the school. Vane demanded to enter the school and have a drink, threathing a droid. Karga refused to Vane's request, and Vane reminded him that the school was a saloon built from Shard's treasure. Karga shot Vane's blaster, and killed Vane's companions with the assistance of Djarin. They let Vane go.<ref name="Chapter 17" /> Gorian Shard later arrived to the planet and took control of the city and the school. Gorian Shard's gang turned the school back to a cantina.<ref name="Chapter 21" />

